#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:4
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:12
msgid ""
"This page groups failures by what is observed and by the reason code that"
" the node reports. Every refusal, failure and waiting state of a task "
"carries a reason code, in the metadata ``anet.reason`` of the task and in"
" the output of the command-line interface. The sentence and the next step"
" that go with a code are the same in the command line, in MCP tool "
"errors, and on the local A2A interface. The complete table is in :ref"
":`reference-reason-codes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:25
msgid "Diagnosis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:27
msgid ""
"Four commands answer most questions. They are listed in the order in "
"which they are usually used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:30
msgid "``anet status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:31
msgid ""
"The state of the running node: identity, hub join state, delivery, "
"inbound policy, payments, sandbox. The status lines use the sentences of "
"the reason table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:35
msgid "``anet doctor``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:36
msgid ""
"What the node is set up to do and which doors are open. It reads the data"
" directory and checks the configuration, the coding tool integrations, "
"the local A2A interface, the sandbox and the payment configuration. It "
"does not need a running daemon. ``anet doctor --json`` gives the same "
"result in a machine-readable form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:42
msgid "``anet logs [N|--all]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:43
msgid "The last ``N`` lines of the daemon log, or the whole log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:45
msgid "``anet task get <task-id> [--full] [--history N]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:46
msgid ""
"One task as it is now, with the reason code in its metadata. ``--full`` "
"returns content that other interfaces cut."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:56
msgid ""
"A code that has a command as its next step is resolved by running that "
"command; the tables below repeat the command where one exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:59
msgid "The meaning of the classes in the tables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:61
msgid "*Refused* (``rejected``): the other side certainly did not run the task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:62
msgid ""
"*Failed* (``failed``): the task ended; the effect on the other side may "
"be unknown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:64
msgid ""
"*Waiting*: the node recovers on its own; no action is needed unless the "
"wait is unusually long."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:66
msgid "*Needs a decision*: the task waits in ``input-required`` for an operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/troubleshooting.rst:67
